rlw@ida.org (Richard Wexelblat) writes:
>Foo has been used as a "throwaway" or temporary name at least since the
>early Interlisp days.  I certainly remember it from the 1970s.  It's one
>half of foo-bar, a misspelling of FUBAR, a WW-II term whose Bowdlerized
>definition is "fouled up beyond recognition".  Those with a cruder turn
>of phrase will easily supply a more lurid first word.

